  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Beaver Ranch is the mountain course Denver players drive 40 minutes for — 21 holes nestled into the Colorado Rockies at Conifer, with challenging terrain, beautiful views, and three full tee sets that turn the same 21 holes into easy, medium, and hard versions of themselves.",
    "The shortest set plays 4,745 feet at par 63; the long set stretches past 7,500 feet at par 65. It's pay to play with camping nearby and a separate 20-hole Bluebird course on the same property — a full mountain disc golf weekend in one place.",
    "The elevation is real and so is the terrain. Bring grippy shoes, a full bag, and a camera."
  ],
