  "signatureHoleDescription": "Hole 21 is the longest in the short set at 301 feet — the hole that sums up Beaver Ranch's mountain character. The pines frame a fairway that falls away toward the valley, and the thin air lets your disc fly a little further than it has any right to. It's the last hole, the best view, and the reason people come back.",
  "localTips": "Pay to play with three tee sets — the easy set is a friendly mountain round, the hard set is a monster. Camping is nearby, and the separate Bluebird course makes it a full weekend. The altitude is real: drink water, throw discs, enjoy the views.",
